# ---- GOLDEN FIXTURE (bridge tile) ----
# resetMode=loadvm -> restore the INTERNAL 'golden' snapshot: X + Open SIMH's
# pdp11 with the VT11 vector display, at the first seconds of a fresh lunar
# descent. The program restarts itself after every crash, so the bake rides its
# own loop: scripts/build-guests/gt40.sh waits for the "NO SURVIVORS" message
# and then for the restart it triggers, and bakes there. A visitor who presses
# reset therefore gets a NEW GAME from 18000 feet with a full tank, not the
# middle of somebody else's doomed trajectory.
SH_RESET_MODE=loadvm
SH_GOLDEN_SNAPSHOT=golden
SH_FIXTURE_DESC=DEC GT40 (1973) at the first seconds of a fresh lunar descent: the LEM in the upper left with its descent engine firing, four telemetry readouts across the top (HEIGHT ~17000-19000 feet, DISTANCE ~-15000 to -21000, VER VEL ~-490, HOR VEL ~880 — the exact digits differ by a second or two of flight from bake to bake), the 75% throttle bar and the two pairs of rotation arrows down the right edge, the twelve-item telemetry menu (HEIGHT, ALTITUDE, DISTANCE, FUEL LEFT, WEIGHT, THRUST, ANGLE, VER VEL, HOR VEL, VER ACC, HOR ACC, SECONDS) under them, and the mountainous lunar horizon across the bottom — green vectors on black, drawn by Open SIMH's VT11 at crt=vr17 scale=1 hspace=narrow in a 1024x1024 SDL window centred on a 1280x1024 X root. The exhibit is self-sustaining: the LEM falls for about two minutes, crashes, and the program restarts itself, a 135 s loop. LIGHT-PEN exhibit: the menu, the rotation arrows and the throttle bar are all selected by pointing; there is no keyboard input of any kind.

# ---- INPUT ----
# The VT11 light pen is Open SIMH's mouse button 1 and nothing else
# (display/sim_ws.c ws_poll: display_lp_sw = mev.b1_state), so the pen is on the
# glass only WHILE the button is held, at the position carried by that same
# event. A press IS the gesture — there is no hover, and a click that lands
# anywhere without a vector under it simply does nothing.
#
# NO KEY PACING KNOBS. Every other bridge tile sets SH_KEY_MIN_HOLD_MS /
# SH_KEY_MIN_GAP_MS because its emulator samples a key matrix once per emulated
# frame. This machine has no keyboard to pace: the 1973 Lunar Lander reads the
# light pen and nothing else, so the tile takes the shared fleet streamhost
# binary with no canary build.

# ---- IDLE PAUSE MATTERS MORE HERE THAN ON ANY OTHER TILE ----
# This is the one exhibit that never sits still: the 1973 tape busy-spins, so
# the simulator costs a measured 177 % of a core (2-vCPU guest, 758 MB host
# QEMU RSS) whether or not anybody is looking at it. The daemon's default
# 60-second freeze is therefore left ON — explicitly, so nobody "helpfully"
# copies amiga's SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=0 here. Pause is not loadvm: guest RAM and
# device state are untouched and the next visitor thaws mid-descent, sub-second.
SH_IDLE_PAUSE_SECS=60
